	(text_box "[${#}] ${TITLE}"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 133.35 15 0)
		(size 162.56 20)
		(margins 5.9999 5.9999 5.9999 5.9999)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 8 8)
				(thickness 1.2)
				(bold yes)
				(color 162 22 34 1)
			)
		)
		(uuid "2f57d04a-e792-4267-9a5a-a708432bf392")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE:\nThe pass PMOSFET is used as a high-side load disconnect controlled by EN_OK. When EN_OK is high, the NPN gate driver pulls the PMOS gate low, turning the\ndevice on. VOUT then tracks VPROT with a small R_{DS,on} drop.\nWhen EN_OK is low, the NPN gate driver is off and the PMOS gate is pulled up towards its source, turning the device off and isolating the load.\nA 1Meg resistor from VOUT to GND provides a defined discharge path and prevents the output node floating when the pass device is off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 520.7 68.58 0)
		(size 63.5 30.48)
		(margins 2 2 2 2)
		(stroke
			(width 1)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "335dfe34-cd29-40bd-8909-6a794014737d")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE:\nThe over-current trip points are 1A and 5A, with 20m shunt.\n\nAt 1A, V_{SHUNT} = I * R_{SHUNT} = 1A * 20m = 20mV\nAt 5A, V_{SHUNT} = I * R_{SHUNT} = 5A * 20m = 100mV"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 267.97 27.94 0)
		(size 41.91 16.51)
		(margins 2 2 2 2)
		(stroke
			(width 1)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4621ce98-5a24-4ba5-a527-078bdc5f178c")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE:\nThe gate driver NPN must meet V_{CE} stress in the off state. With VPROT up to 50 V, the NPN can see effectively 50 V across C-E.\n\nBC846 VCEO = 65 V is functional but has limited margin (FoS = 1.3). A higher voltage small-signal NPN is recommended to improve robustness."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 515.62 36.83 0)
		(size 46.99 26.67)
		(margins 2 2 2 2)
		(stroke
			(width 1)
			(type solid)
			(color 250 236 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "500c678a-4f82-4a53-927e-ca7b2365a95a")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE:\nBC846 provides low-side gate drive for the pass PMOS gate.\nA 10k base resistor limits base drive from EN_OK. A 100k base-emitter resistor ensures a defined off state during start-up and fault conditions by discharging base charge and preventing a floating base."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 519.43 105.41 0)
		(size 63.5 26.67)
		(margins 2 2 2 2)
		(stroke
			(width 1)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5eca3288-88a3-4227-8a43-7e3ec58dd0d0")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE:\nThis PMOS is acting as an ideal diode [1].\n\nA 10 V zener from gate to source limits V_{GS} ≤ 10 V under all VIN and transient conditions to protect the PMOS. A 100k gate to source resistor stops the gate floating. A 100k gate pulldown resistor sets default state to OFF when no voltage at VIN is present."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 29.21 20.32 0)
		(size 38.1 24.13)
		(margins 2 2 2 2)
		(stroke
			(width 1)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "789af0e8-f050-41ec-8d28-5094829c8e8e")
	)
	(text_box "LAYOUT NOTE:\nWe'll size for 5A current on 35um trace. We'll pick 3.5mm for a 25% margin. Keep traces short and wide, use pours/puddles when possible."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 314.96 27.94 0)
		(size 30.48 16.51)
		(margins 2.25 2.25 2.25 2.25)
		(stroke
			(width 1.5)
			(type solid)
			(color 0 0 255 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 0 255 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9c8daeb4-17a1-41d3-befd-72628e07166b")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE:\nCurrent is measured using INA169 with R_{SHUNT} = 20m.\n\nWith R_{L} = 15k, the output voltage is:\nV_{OUT} = I * R_{SHUNT} * (R_{L} / 1k)\n\nAt 1A: V_{OUT} = 1A * 20m * (15k / 1k) = 0.30V\nAt 5A: V_{OUT} = 5A * 20m * (15k / 1k) = 1.50V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 274.32 102.87 0)
		(size 34.29 25.4)
		(margins 2 2 2 2)
		(stroke
			(width 1)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a4c75254-2c59-4613-8699-ac6763cb7409")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE:\nThe lockout delay is set by an RC network with R = 432k and C = 4.7u.\n\nThe time constant is: τ = R * C ≈ 432k * 4.7u ≈ 2s\n\nAfter a fault the capacitor must recharge before the circuit rearms, creating a ~2s lockout period."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 29.21 265.43 0)
		(size 53.34 20.32)
		(margins 2 2 2 2)
		(stroke
			(width 1)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ad0fd7b2-7db9-4a80-9c91-6055f1ec750b")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE:\nA capacitor pre-charge diode rapidly charges the timing capacitor at\nstartup, ensuring the lockout circuit begins in the armed state and\npreventing a false startup delay."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 194.31 0)
		(size 33.02 16.51)
		(margins 2 2 2 2)
		(stroke
			(width 1)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bad5df7f-2e13-4a7c-900f-f118f36ce4e6")
	)
	(text_box "LAYOUT NOTE:\nRoute HI LO leads short from shunt to current amplifier."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 214.63 34.29 0)
		(size 30.48 10.16)
		(margins 2.25 2.25 2.25 2.25)
		(stroke
			(width 1.5)
			(type solid)
			(color 0 0 255 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 0 255 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cbf7568e-5bf2-4d52-aed6-01dd01e61498")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE:\nPer TI [2], choose the series resistor R_{S} such that I_{RMIN} < I_{R} < I_{RMAX} across the full input range, while supplying the worst-case load current from VCC_5V.\nAssume:\nV_{IN,MIN} = 12 V, V_{IN,MAX} = 50 V, V_{OUT} = 5 V\nI_{RMAX} = 15 mA, I_{RMIN} = 75 uA\nWorst-case VCC_5V load current with EN_OK high is estimated as:\nI_{LOAD,MAX} = I_{DIV,2V5} + I_{Q,LM393} + I_{Q,INA169} + I_{B,NPN}\nwhere:\nI_{DIV,2V5} = 5 V / (100k + 100k) = 25 uA\nI_{Q,LM393} = 2 * 600 µA = 1.2 mA (two LM393 packages)\nI_{Q,INA169} = 125 uA\nI_{B,NPN} = (5 V − 0.7 V) / 10k = 430 uA\nNote:\nThe fault LED current is drawn only when EN_OK is low and is therefore not included in the EN_OK-high load budget.\nThus:\nI_{LOAD,MAX} = 25 uA + 1.2 mA + 125 uA + 430 uA = 1.78 mA\nThis gives:\nR_{S,MAX} = (V_{IN,MIN} − V_{OUT}) / (I_{LOAD,MAX} + I_{RMIN}) = 7 V / (1.78 mA + 0.075 mA) = 3.8k\nR_{S,MIN} = (V_{IN,MAX} − V_{OUT}) / I_{RMAX} = 45 V / 15 mA = 3k\nR_{S} (R403) is selected as 3.32k to ensure regulation at V_{IN,MIN} while limiting shunt current at V_{IN,MAX}.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 619.76 35.56 0)
		(size 67.31 68.58)
		(margins 2 2 2 2)
		(stroke
			(width 1)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e44be17e-4765-4bb9-9fa8-6a1035b4166e")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE:\nRC low-pass filters are placed on each VSENSE input to reduce noise and minimise chatter. The filters have a cutoff frequency of:\nf_{c} = 1 / (2π * 1k * 10n) = 16 Hz.\nPositive feedback resistors provide hysteresis to again reduce chatter. Capacitor placement in accordance with 6.11 [3]."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 538.48 175.26 0)
		(size 64.77 19.05)
		(margins 2 2 2 2)
		(stroke
			(width 1)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e4f1e7bf-6b1d-4c1c-b72b-b9f0bc7b400a")
	)
